 "note": "On 5 August 1395 two new ṭāʾifas are carved from the lands won at the Peace of Ramaḍān and given to the Emperor's cousins, sons of his late uncles: Shalamanka (21 towns of the Leonese west) to Saʿd ibn Ismāʿīl, and Qūnka (20 towns of the Castilian east) to Saʿd ibn Faraj, the Emperor's son-in-law. Madrid, Cáceres and all the Portuguese lands stay with the crown. The realm holds 148 towns and 1,742,000 people directly, with six ṭāʾifas; the game ranks it seventh. The treasury stands at 158, with 565 still owed; stability has fallen to 9.5. The same day the Dīwān al-Inshāʾ completes the bureaucracy. Shares of power are estimated from the 1 June 1349 reading.",
